          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em CW-spectrum
            is the analogue for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            of the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
          %p
            Just like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
            are cofibrant objects in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+model+category"} stable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra"} model structure on topological sequential spectra
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Cofibrancy"} below
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_components In components
          #CWSpectrum.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong CW-spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet\in SeqSpec(Top)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectrum"} sequential spectrum
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  all component spaces
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n
                  are
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
              %li
                %p
                  all structure maps
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma X_n \longrightarrow X_{n+1}
                  are inclusions of subcomplexes
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#Adams74"}> Adams 74, p. 139
            ) Beware that for instance (
            %a{:href => "#Switzer75"}> Switzer 75, def. 8.1
            ) says just “spectrum” for “CW-spectrum”.
          %p
            For a CW-spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            there is a concept of “cell of a spectrum”:
          #CellOfACWSpectrum.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong cell
              of a CW-spectrum, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CWSpectrum"}
              is a cell of one of the components CW-complexes
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mo &gt;
                          %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{\gt n}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n-1}
          %p
            This way every CW-spectrum is the union of all its cells in the sense of def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CellOfACWSpectrum"}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Switzer75"} Switzer 75, 8.4
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A CW-spectrum, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CWSpectrum"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+spectrum"} finite spectrum
              (or countable spectrum, etc.) if it has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finitely many
              cells (countably many cells) according to def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CellOfACWSpectrum"}
          %h3#via_spectrum_attaching_maps Via spectrum attaching maps
          #SphereSpectrumOfIntegerDimension.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}
              (possibly negative) define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}^n
              to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+prespectrum"} sequential prespectrum
              with component spaces
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mrow
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo +
                                  %mi n
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi k
                              %mo +
                              %mi n
                              %mo ≥
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mi otherwise
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mathbb{S}^{n})_k
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    S^{k+n} &amp; if \; k + n \geq 0
                    \\\
                    \\ast &amp; otherwise
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p and with structure maps the canonical isomorphisms.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LewisMaySteinberger86"}> Lewis-May-Steinberger 86, def. 4.3
            )
          .num_defn
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SphereSpectrumOfIntegerDimension"}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
                  then
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi Σ
                          %mn ∞
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}^0 = \mathbb{S} = \Sigma^\infty S^0
                  is standard sequential incarnation of the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq n
                  then
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mi n
                        %mo ≃
                        %msup
                          %mi Σ
                          %mn ∞
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}^n \simeq \Sigma^\infty S^n
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
                  on the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
              %li
                %p
                  for general
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  then
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mi n
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi n
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}^n \simeq F_{-n} S^0
                  is also known as the
                  = succeed "th" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-n)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+spectrum"} free spectrum
                  on
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+spectrum"} cell spectrum
              is a topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectrum"} sequential spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              realized as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              over a sequence of spectra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast = X_0 \to X_1 \to X_2 \to X_3 \to \cdots
              such that there are morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo ⊔
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi n
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi q
                            %mi n
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    j_n
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{i \in I_n}{\sqcup} \mathbb{S}^{q_n}
                    \\right)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    X_n
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n+1}= Cone(j_n)
              (the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#StrictModelStructureCellAttachmentToSpectra"}> rmk.
              )
            %p
              A cell spectrum is a
              %strong CW-spectrum
              if each attaching map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi q
                          %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty S^{q_n}\to X_n
              factors through a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_k \to X_n
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \lt q
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#LewisMaySteinberger86"} Lewis-May-Steinberger 86, def. 5.1, def. 5.2
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Weiss"} Weiss
          %h3#category_of_cwspectra Category of CW-spectra
          %p
            There is an obvious category of CW-spectra given as the full subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CWSpec
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CWSpec'
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SeqSpec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(Top)
            consisting of the CW-spectra, ie. a morphism of CW-spectra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X \to Y
            is given by levelwise maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n: X_n \to F_n
            that are compatible with the structure maps. In accordance with
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "Switzer75"} Switzer 75, 8.9
            = succeed "." do
              %strong functions
          %p However, often there is a more useful notion of morphisms between CW-spectra.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              be a CW-spectrum. A
              %strong subspectrum
              is a CW spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              such that each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_n
              is a subcomplex of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
              %strong cofinal
              if for each cell
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_n \in E_n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi m
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^m e_n \in F_{n + m}
          %p
            We can then construct the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CWSpec
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CWSpec
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CWSpec
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CWSpec'
            at the cofinal inclusions. Since the class of cofinal inclusions admit a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+right+fractions"} calculus of right fractions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CWSpec
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CWSpec
            has the following concrete description - a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CWSpec
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CWSpec
            is given by a function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{X} \to Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{X}
            is some cofinal subspectrum of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: \tilde{X} \to Y
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                  %mo :
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f': \tilde{X}' \to Y
            are considered equivalent if there is some further cofinal subspectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo ″
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo ∩
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{X}'' \subseteq \tilde{X} \cap \tilde{X'}
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo ″
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f|_{\tilde{X}'} = f'|_{\tilde{X}''}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#Cofibrancy Cofibrancy
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectrum"} sequential spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in SeqSpec(Top)_{stable}
              is cofibrant in the stable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra"} model structure on topological sequential spectra
              in particular if all component spaces are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complexes"} cell complexes
              and all its structure morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \wedge X_n \to X_{n+1}
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complexes"} relative cell complexes
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-spectra"} CW-spectra
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CellOfACWSpectrum"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SeqSpec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Top
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(Top)_{stable}
          %p
            For the proof see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra#CellSpectraAreCofibrantInModelStructureOnTopologicalSequentialSpectra"} there
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in SeqSpec(Top)_{stable}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-spectrum"} CW-spectrum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+spectrum"} cylinder spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \wedge (I_+)
              is a
              %em good
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \vee X \longrightarrow X \wedge (I_+)
            %p
              is a cofibration in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SeqSpec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Top
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(Top)_{stable}
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra#CylinderSpectrumOverCWSpectrumIsGood"} this prop.
          %h3#CWApproximation CW-approximation
          %p
            The analog of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-approximation"} CW-approximation
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            holds true for topological
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in SeqSpec(Top)
              a topological
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectrum"} sequential spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+weak+homotopy+equivalence"} stable weak homotopy equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat X \longrightarrow X
                    \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#ElmendorfKrizMay95"} Elmendorf-Kriz-May 95, theorem 1.5
          .proof
            %h6#proof_1 Proof 1
            %p
              First let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X_0 \longrightarrow X_0
              be a CW-approximation of the component space in degree 0, via
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "CW+approximation#CWApproximationForContinuousFunctions"} this prop.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-approximation"} CW-approximation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_{k \leq n} \colon  \hat X_{k \leq n} \to X_{k \leq n}
              has been found such that all the structure maps are respected. Consider then the continuous function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi n
                    %mi Σ
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Sigma \hat X_n \overset{\Sigma \phi_n}{\longrightarrow} \Sigma X_n \overset{\sigma_n}{\longrightarrow} X_{n+1}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Applying
              %a{:href => "CW+approximation#CWApproximationForContinuousFunctions"} that prop.
              to this function factors it as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Sigma X_n \hookrightarrow \hat X_{n+1} \overset{\phi_{n+1}}{\longrightarrow} X_{n+1}
                    \\,.
            %p Hence we have obtained the next stage of the CW-approximation. The respect for the structure maps is just this factorization property:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Σ
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi Σ
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mi Σ
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mi incl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Sigma \hat X_n
                    \&amp;\overset{\Sigma \phi_n}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\Sigma X_n
                    \\\
                    {}^{incl}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\sigma_n}}
                    \\\
                    \\hat X_{n+1} &amp;\underset{\phi_{n+1}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X_{n+1}
                    }
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof 2
            %p
              A high-powered way to see this is to use the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              between the stable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra"} model structure on topological sequential spectra
              and the stable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield-Friedlander+model+structure"} Bousfield-Friedlander model structure
              (see there) on sequential spectra in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi Q
                      %mi Sing
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mi stable
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert Q Sing X\vert}
                    \\overset{\in W_{stable}}{\longrightarrow}
                    X
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi Sing
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert - \vert} \dashv Sing
              is degreewise the adjunction between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
              and forming
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complex"} singular simplicial complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              denotes any cofibrant replacement in the BF-model structure.
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Adams74
              %p
